  "issue_title": "[strategy] nystrom transform: landmark column sampling for low-rank matmul",
  "issue_body": "## Idea\n\nThe built-in `rsvd` transform builds its basis with four streamed random sketches over `A` and `B` (`~2 N\u00b2 M` FLOPs) plus a thin QR. On genuine **low-rank** couples the column space can be captured by sampling a small set of landmark columns instead \u2014 much cheaper basis construction at held accuracy.\n\nThis proposes a new registered transform **`nystrom`**: split the `M` budget across col(A), row(A), col(B), row(B), gather random landmark columns/rows, then thin-QR into `Q`. Basis cost is essentially the QR (`~2 N M\u00b2`), not rsvd's sketches.\n\n**Measured (RTX 5090, N=12000, M=1500, lowrank data-rank=16):** accuracy **1.0000**, VRAM 713 MiB vs exact 2208 MiB, **2.3\u00d7 fewer FLOPs**, latency 2423 ms vs exact 2301 ms \u2014 so **not admitted** under the one rule (latency \u2265 exact), but faster and cheaper-FLOPs than rsvd at the same accuracy/VRAM.\n\n## Target regime\n\n- Matrix content: low-rank (also holds on decaying-spectrum in measurement)\n- Expected `N`, `M`, dtype, device: N=12000, M=1500, fp32, RTX 5090\n\n## Expected trade-off\n\nAgainst the exact baseline, on `--fill lowrank --data-rank 16` (measured):\n\n| aspect          | vs exact (measured) |\n|-----------------|---------------------|\n| accuracy        | held (1.0000) |\n| time complexity | lower (2.3\u00d7 fewer FLOPs) |\n| latency         | slightly higher (2423 vs 2301 ms) \u2014 blocks admission |\n| VRAM usage      | lower (713 vs 2208 MiB) |\n\n## Notes\n\n- Distinct from `rsvd`: column/row landmarks + QR vs four random sketches.\n- Same accuracy/VRAM as rsvd here, ~2.3\u00d7 lower latency than rsvd (2423 vs 5492 ms).\n",
  "merged_at": "2026-07-13T14:00:56.000Z",
